# The words Polish counts with.
#
# Italian's number rules are 26 of them over nine thousand lines and they cover
# dates, times, money, Roman numerals, ordinals and fractions as well as
# counting. What is being replaced here is only the words: each arm of a
# counting rule calls a wrapper whose name carries the word and its length, so a
# Polish word is a wrapper of ours and one call name changed in the arm. The
# structure -- which arm fires for which digit, how the digits are grouped --
# is Italian's and stays, because grouping into hundreds and thousands is the
# same in both languages.
#
# Each of these is IBM's own wrapper with the symbol and the length changed,
# written as raw lower notation inside a bare rule so that nothing else about
# them can differ from it.

# dwa
rule pol_say_2 takes 3 from glob.obj
  bare
  raw push param 2
  raw push param 1
  raw push param 0
  raw call lpta_rpta_loadp arity 3 depth 3
  raw push imm 0
  raw push sym pol_num_2
  raw push imm 3
  raw push imm 1
  raw push param 0
  raw call insert_2pt_s arity 5 depth 8
  raw popn 8
  raw alu negl none reg r0
  raw alu sbbl reg r0 reg r0
  raw alu negl none reg r0
  raw return reg r0
end

